  "findings": [
    "The fixed sherpa core links kaldi-native-fbank-core (not kaldifeat), kaldi-decoder-core, ssentencepiece_core, ONNX Runtime, fst and fstfar. kaldi-native-fbank pulls the pinned kissfft commit; kaldi-decoder pulls kaldifst, which pulls OpenFST. JSON is included as headers.",
    "The Android static release workflow sets BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=OFF and invokes the Android scripts. The inspected ARM64 script defaults TTS and diarization to ON, disables PortAudio and tests, and links libc++ statically by default.",
    "With TTS enabled, sherpa core links piper_phonemize, which links espeak-ng and ucd. The exact espeak-ng fork README declares GPL version 3 or later; ucd-tools supplies GPL version 3 COPYING. MIT for piper-phonemize does not remove these dependencies.",
    "Read-only scan of the downloaded ARM64 JNI library found /tmp/espeakXXXXXX and OfflineSpeakerDiarization JNI strings. This is supporting static evidence; no native code was executed.",
    "GitHub recursive tree inspection found no root or nested NOTICE file in the fixed sherpa repository or identified dependency repositories; supplied COPYING and LICENSE variants were preserved.",
    "Hedley shipped header declares MIT and authors Niels Lohmann and Evan Nemerson, while the JSON license documentation says CC0-1.0 for Hedley. Both supplied notices were preserved without silently resolving that difference.",
    "The Android-specific simple-sentencepiece CMake patch removes threading/ThreadPool code; darts-clone BSD-2-Clause embedded license remains relevant and was extracted verbatim."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This is not a complete binary SBOM or an attestation of the exact publisher build. Dependencies were inferred from fixed release build sources and supported by limited read-only binary strings.",
    "Supplying licenses alone does not satisfy all GPL distribution obligations such as corresponding source/build and installation information where applicable. No distribution approval or choice of application license is made here. A separate ASR-only runtime build with SHERPA_ONNX_ENABLE_TTS=OFF is a possible future artifact, not the current AAR.",
    "The workflow uses ANDROID_NDK_LATEST_HOME rather than a pinned NDK revision; exact libc++/libc++abi toolchain notices cannot be certified from available release sources. ONNX Runtime aggregated notices include LLVM notices but do not establish the exact NDK runtime license inventory.",
    "No source archives, toolchains or native dependencies were downloaded. Only small license/notice files were recovered. No scripts were executed, and assets/Gradle/application code/state documents were not changed.",
    "The existing sherpa, ORT MIT, Silero MIT and NVIDIA CC-BY-4.0 texts/attribution remain separately required; this manifest supplements rather than replaces recursos-manifest.json and fuentes-manifest.json."
  ]
}
